    <string name="hero_preparing">Starting</string>
    <string name="hero_preparing_text">Looking for a way to run as root.</string>
    <string name="hero_no_privilege">Root is needed</string>
    <string name="hero_no_privilege_text">Replay Integrity configures the keystore simulator and the build spoof in /data/adb, which only root can do. Set up one of the ways below.</string>
    <string name="hero_restricted">Root is restricted</string>
    <string name="hero_restricted_text">The root manager runs this application as root without the capabilities of root, so nothing can be changed. Grant it full root access (in Magisk: Superuser → Grant instead of Restrict; in KernelSU: the app profile).</string>
    <string name="hero_checking">Checking</string>
    <string name="hero_checking_text">Reading the keybox, the fingerprint and the modules.</string>
    <string name="hero_not_set_up">Not set up yet</string>
    <string name="hero_not_set_up_text">Set up downloads a keybox and a fingerprint, configures both modules and installs the boot hook.</string>
    <string name="hero_ready">Ready for STRONG</string>
    <string name="hero_ready_text">The keybox, the fingerprint and both modules are in place, and they are kept valid.</string>
    <string name="hero_attention">Needs attention</string>
    <string name="hero_attention_text">Something in the checklist below keeps Play Integrity from reaching STRONG.</string>
    <string name="setup_title">Ways to get root</string>
    <string name="setup_help">Use su of Magisk, KernelSU or APatch (choose \"Grant\" when asked; in KernelSU, allow this application in the manager first), Sui, or Shizuku started with root. Shizuku started through wireless debugging or ADB runs as the shell user, which cannot write /data/adb.</string>
    <string name="grant">Grant</string>
    <string name="check_again">Check again</string>
    <string name="restricted_title">Root is restricted</string>
    <string name="restricted_text">su runs this application as root, but the root manager has removed the capabilities of root, so the configuration can be neither read nor changed. In Magisk, open Superuser and change the access of Replay Integrity from \"Restrict\" to \"Grant\". Other root managers have similar settings, such as the app profile of KernelSU.</string>
